WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:02.840
- And then to top this
all off, my bar mitzvah.

00:00:02.840 --> 00:00:04.410
I was Jewish.

00:00:04.410 --> 00:00:05.243
Am Jewish.

00:00:05.243 --> 00:00:06.227
- Oh, I was like, were you?

00:00:06.227 --> 00:00:07.060
Are you now or?

00:00:07.060 --> 00:00:07.893
- Yes.

00:00:09.308 --> 00:00:10.650
- Look at you!

00:00:10.650 --> 00:00:11.880
- Oh, there I am!

00:00:11.880 --> 00:00:12.880
- You're so cute.

00:00:12.880 --> 00:00:14.293
- I was so fat.

00:00:15.450 --> 00:00:17.310
- Well, once again, we went opposite.

00:00:17.310 --> 00:00:19.132
I'm now fatter.

00:00:19.132 --> 00:00:21.058
We went opposite.

00:00:21.058 --> 00:00:21.891
What was your bar mitzvah like?

00:00:21.891 --> 00:00:24.370
- So, I didn't really care about
the religious part so much,

00:00:24.370 --> 00:00:26.530
but I really cared about the party.

00:00:26.530 --> 00:00:27.870
I was obsessed with the party,

00:00:27.870 --> 00:00:31.270
and, you know, every bar mitzvah
party had this big theme.

00:00:31.270 --> 00:00:35.470
And so the theme of mine,
because I couldn't decide,

00:00:35.470 --> 00:00:39.770
was Broadway meets pop music.

00:00:39.770 --> 00:00:43.250
Which, one gay man
laughed, in this audience.

00:00:43.250 --> 00:00:44.710
Which is an odd theme.

00:00:44.710 --> 00:00:46.100
What does that even mean?

00:00:46.100 --> 00:00:47.160
There was a like a

00:00:48.144 --> 00:00:51.580
life-sized cutout of Madonna

00:00:51.580 --> 00:00:53.480
on one side of the DJ booth.

00:00:53.480 --> 00:00:55.930
There are tears in your eyes right now.

00:00:55.930 --> 00:00:57.900
And on the other side of the DJ booth,

00:00:57.900 --> 00:00:59.220
and this is not an exaggeration,

00:00:59.220 --> 00:01:02.696
was a life-sized cutout of
The Phantom of the Opera.

00:01:02.696 --> 00:01:03.753
- That was the first musical I ever saw.

00:01:03.753 --> 00:01:06.010
- Which I was obsessed with at the time.

00:01:06.010 --> 00:01:07.900
And all the kid's tables were named

00:01:07.900 --> 00:01:10.350
after pop stars that I loved at the time.

00:01:10.350 --> 00:01:11.820
I sat at the Madonna table.

00:01:11.820 --> 00:01:13.200
There was a George Michael table.

00:01:13.200 --> 00:01:15.283
Aerosmith for the straight boys.

00:01:16.936 --> 00:01:18.970
And then all the adult tables

00:01:18.970 --> 00:01:20.640
were named after Broadway shows.

00:01:20.640 --> 00:01:21.473
- It was rock and roll.

00:01:21.473 --> 00:01:22.306
They might have been open.

00:01:22.306 --> 00:01:23.139
You never know.

00:01:23.139 --> 00:01:23.972
- Exactly.

00:01:24.880 --> 00:01:27.153
And that was my crazy childhood.

